Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
The MAE is defined as the average of the absolute difference between forecasted and actual values. The actual battery capacity at an instant of time i is 𝑦(battery_capacity)i, and the predicted value at the same instant of time i is 𝑦(battery_capacity)i. The error term here is 𝑦(battery_capacity)i - 𝑦(battery_capacity)i. The error term’s magnitude can be positive or negative depending on the predicted value. However, for calculating the MAE, we take the average of the absolute difference between the actual and predicted values. The total number of samples here is N. This is as explained in the equation below,
